  "dataset_path": "evaluation/dataset.json",
  "note": "Focused 30-run single-pattern batch for the final research benchmark: the hierarchical pattern only, blackboard context sharing only, on 24 distinct prompts (12 core + 12 breadth) plus 6 repeats of core prompts. Twelve categories, each represented twice in core+breadth. It is a deliberate subset of the 72-run matrix in evaluation/config.json and of the 36-run plan in evaluation/hierarchical_36.json; both are preserved unchanged. Seeds are null because athena.run forwards no seed to any provider, so the variance tier is a stochastic replicate and its spread is sampling noise. Live runs use --backend subprocess: the in_process backend redirects this process's stdout/stderr, which breaks MCP stdio toolset spawning. RUNTIME COPY for the amd profile (openai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash at api.tokenlab.amd.com): the 30 plan entries, prompt selection, tiers, categories, seed-null interpretation, backend and all call/token caps are unchanged. Only the per-run timeout (1200->3600 s) and total wall budget (86400->172800 s) were raised for AMD latency; budget.max_runs remains 36 (30 scheduled keys + at most 6 transient-retry attempts), and no USD cap is enforceable because the endpoint publishes no price. V2 correction (pre-dataset, after independent audit): the historical .env ATHENA_MAX_LLM_CALLS=12 is a stale Groq diagnostic override and silently replaced the documented hierarchical policy of 40 calls (athena.config.caps PATTERN_CAPS). The runtime launcher now exports ATHENA_MAX_LLM_CALLS=40 to the runner, every athena.run child, and the CrewAI server, and this config records llm_call_cap=40. Provider call timeout is 900 s and the A2A role timeout 1200 s, under the unchanged 3600 s per-run wall. Token caps, critic/security thresholds, retry classification and the 36-attempt cap are unchanged.",
